A||||14||88CoupeV6||Proof that seatbelts really work||||4||
Z||000000||88CoupeV6||06-14-2001||05:27 PM||||Here are some pics that prove that seatbelts save lives. One of my drivers was driving this on I-495 and hit a pothole. The truck started fishtailing and lost its balance and turned sideways. it flipped 3 times and hit some trees landing on its roof. The driver was only doing 50-55 MPH in a 65. He only got a bruise from hanging from his seatbelt LUCKY Guy. The state is now fixing and repaving the road because it has been such a hazard in that area.<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1249362&a=13266270&p=50355260&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1249362&a=13266270&p=50355264&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1249362&a=13266270&p=50355258&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||4
Z||000001||GOLDSE||06-14-2001||05:30 PM||||Lucky guy indeed!  Now, I'll never get those parts delivered.||||reg||7
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||06-14-2001||05:31 PM||||The good part is that he was on his way back to the building after his route.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||06-14-2001||05:47 PM||||I was having a conversation with a friend about seatbelts last Saturday. He reported that his brother was in a roll over accident and was not wearing a seatbelt. He said it was a good thing because the roof had collapsed. I said Oh really, Its a good thing it landed on it's roof and stayed there. If it had kept on rolling there is a good chance he would have been ejected from the car and possibly killed. There was a long silence and he really didn't have much to say about the subject after that.||||reg||14
Z||000004||p4n1c||06-14-2001||07:22 PM||||Actually a friend of mine was lucky he was ejected from his Firebird.  It rolled over a few times, he was taken to the hospital with minor injuries.  He went and saw the car a couple weeks later and the car had destroyed and the t-top middle support had basically wrapped around the steering column, it would've crushed him if he had've been in the car.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||06-14-2001||07:53 PM||||No he was not lucky to be ejected from the car. He was lucky he was not partially ejected and have the car crush his upper or lower half as it rolled over. That is definatly luck.<p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||p4n1c||06-14-2001||08:05 PM||||Well in that case he was lucky from both situations.. He was lucky to be ejected rather then having the t-top support wrap around his body and kill him.  And he was lucky he landed away from the car.  But this is one situation where it was better to have not been wearing it.  Seatbelts are not save alls, they are damn good to have and will end up saving more lives then killing, but they are not the end all of safety.  <P>And before you ask if I wear mine, the answer is yes, everytime my a$$ hits the seat and I'm ready to move.||||reg||1
